course: dictionary
lesson: 12822
title: Medicine words: emetic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emetic is a medicine or substance that makes a person be sick, which means vomit. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «Long ago, the doctor gave the sick sailor an emetic.» The sailor was then sick. So an emetic makes you sick, and it is a medical word, so it belongs in stories about hospitals and old medicine.
explain: Emetic can also be an adjective, which describes a thing. «The old doctor gave him an emetic drug.» Here emetic describes the drug, so it tells you what sort of drug it was.
fact: An emetic makes a person vomit, which means be sick.
fact: Emetic can be a noun, as in «an emetic», or an adjective, as in «an emetic drug».
fact: Long ago, doctors sometimes used emetics against poisoning, but doctors now rarely use them.
fact: Never make someone sick after they have swallowed poison unless a doctor says so.
fact: If someone has swallowed something harmful, call for help straight away and follow the advice of the adults and doctors.
exercise: «The old doctor gave the sailor an emetic.» What is an emetic? | A cool drink for hot days | A bandage for a cut | *A medicine that makes a person be sick | A medicine that helps you sleep
exercise: «Never make someone sick after they swallow poison, unless a doctor says so.» What should you do first? | Give them more to drink | Let them sleep it off | Make them be sick straight away | *Call for help and wait for a doctor's advice
exercise: In «an emetic drug», what kind of word is emetic? | *An adjective | An adverb | A verb | A noun
test: Long ago, doctors sometimes used emetics against what? | Sunburn | *Poisoning | A broken bone | A cold
test: Which sentence is true? | *Doctors now rarely use emetics | Emetics make you grow taller | Emetics are a kind of sweet | Doctors use emetics every day
exam: A child has swallowed poison. What is the safest first step? | Wait an hour to see if it passes | Let the child sleep it off | Make the child be sick at home | *Call for help straight away and do not make them sick unless a doctor says so
